      "title": "‘I’ve killed someone’: Beau Lamarre-Condon allegedly confessed to friend and asked for help moving bodies, court told",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/23/beau-lamarre-condon-allegedly-confessed-to-friend-murder-trial-court-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Friend tells jury Lamarre-Condon told him in early 2024 ‘I shot the first one through the head and the second one through the door’</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Beau Lamarre-Condon allegedly confessed to killing two men, telling his friend it was an “out-of-body experience”, before attempting to play it off as a joke, a court has been told.</p><p>Lamarre-Condon, 31, is accused of fatally shooting couple Jesse Baird and Luke Davies with his police service weapon in Baird’s Paddington home on 19 February 2024.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/23/beau-lamarre-condon-allegedly-confessed-to-friend-murder-trial-court-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
