      "title": "Embattled Queensland minister Amanda Camm quits Crisafulli frontbench citing health and safety reasons",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/23/embattled-qld-mininster-amanda-camm-quits-crisafulli-frontbench-citing-health-and-safety-reasons",
      "description": "<p>Camm, who resigned following months of pressure over her handling of state’s child safety system, cited Helen Haines attack as reason for departure</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">new political email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>The Queensland minister Amanda Camm has resigned from cabinet following months of pressure over the state government’s handling of the child safety system and efforts to prevent domestic and family violence.</p><p>Camm told reporters on Friday the decision to step down was “mine alone”.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/23/embattled-qld-mininster-amanda-camm-quits-crisafulli-frontbench-citing-health-and-safety-reasons\">Continue reading...</a>",
