      "title": "Australia offers astronaut Katherine Bennell-Pegg for space mission to International Space Station",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/23/australian-astronaut-katherine-bennell-pegg-2028-space-mission",
      "description": "<p>Australian of the Year would become the first astronaut in space to qualify under the Australian flag if she embarks on the 2028 mission</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>The federal government has sent an offer to the European Space Agency (ESA) to send the Australian of the Year, astronaut Katherine Bennell-Pegg, to the International Space Station.</p><p>The mission, slated for 2028, will mark the first time a qualified astronaut has flown to space under the Australian flag.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/23/australian-astronaut-katherine-bennell-pegg-2028-space-mission\">Continue reading...</a>",
